        "Content": "TEAM SCOTT WINSLADE AND PATRICK LEONARD | THE DUBLIN 10 PROPERTY SPECIALISTS\r\n\r\n2 BED 1 BATH FULLY EXTENDED SINGLE STOREY COTTAGE STYLE RESIDENCE\r\n\r\nLOW MAINTENANCE SOUTH FACING COURTYARD \r\n\r\nLeonard Wilson Keenan Estate Agency are delighted to present No. 3 Liffey Street South, Dublin 10, a charming and deceptively spacious fully extended two-bedroom cottage-style residence ideally positioned in one of the area's most convenient and well-connected locations.\r\n\r\nBehind its attractive original red brick façade and traditional cottage appearance lies a wonderfully bright and well-maintained home that has been thoughtfully extended to maximise living accommodation while retaining its unique character and appeal.\r\n\r\nThe accommodation comprises an inviting entrance leading directly into a generously proportioned living room. Flooded with natural light and presented in crisp contemporary white décor, this impressive living space offers a warm and welcoming atmosphere and is further enhanced by a feature fireplace, creating an ideal focal point for everyday living and entertaining alike.\r\n\r\nTo the front of the property, a spacious double bedroom enjoys excellent natural light and generous proportions. The kitchen is positioned to the rear and offers a practical layout with all essential appliances and a range of cleverly designed storage solutions. Beyond the kitchen lies the fully tiled family bathroom, located within the rear extension and complete with shower facilities. Carefully considered glass panels allow an abundance of natural light to enter while maintaining complete privacy.\r\n\r\nThe rear of the property opens onto a low-maintenance south-facing courtyard, a wonderful outdoor space that enjoys sunshine throughout the day. The courtyard further benefits from access to a private rear laneway, adding both convenience and practicality.\r\n\r\nAdditional features include gas-fired central heating, on-street parking available in abundance and a property presented in good condition throughout, allowing the successful purchaser to move in immediately with minimal fuss.\r\n\r\nThe location is simply exceptional. Memorial Park is literally a stone's throw from the front door, offering extensive green spaces ideal for walking, jogging, cycling and enjoying the outdoors. The highly regarded Ruby Finnegan's traditional public house is situated at the end of the road, while local sporting and leisure amenities including a pitch and putt course are right on the doorstep.\r\n\r\nThe property enjoys unrivalled connectivity with multiple access routes to Dublin City Centre and immediate convenience to the M50 motorway network, making commuting straightforward regardless of destination. A host of local shops, schools, transport links and amenities are all within easy reach.\r\n\r\nNo. 3 Liffey Street South represents an excellent opportunity for first-time buyers, downsizers and investors alike to acquire a charming home in a mature and highly sought-after residential setting.\r\n\r\nEarly viewing is strongly advised.\r\n\r\n*All information provided is to the best of our knowledge. The utmost care and attention has been taken to provide accurate and reliable details. Some information may have been supplied by the vendor. Leonard Wilson Keenan Estate & Letting Agents accept no responsibility for any errors, omissions, or inaccuracies in our marketing material and encourage all interested parties to satisfy themselves as to the correctness of the information provided.*"
      },
